&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Engineering Manager, Rapid Response Assignment - UK&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Location: Remote (Cheltenham, UK)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Team: Product &amp;amp; Engineering&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Employment Type: Full-Time&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About VulnCheck&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Exploitation prevention is only as strong as the intelligence driving those efforts, and most of the industry is still running on intelligence that lacks exploit context. VulnCheck, The Exploit Intelligence Company, delivers structured exploit intelligence on what is actively weaponized in the wild, purpose-built for the data lakes, ETL pipelines, automation, and AI and LLM workflows your infrastructure already runs on, raising the capability of everything it powers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for an Engineering Manager to lead our Rapid Response organization - regionally-based teams in the US, UK, and APAC that keep our customers unblocked around the clock. You’ll manage engineering teams of senior ICs directly, set the technical and operational bar for the group, and make sure work is prioritised correctly across a demanding mix of urgent and long-term needs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This team sits at the intersection of Engineering, Customer Success, and Sales. Your teams handle urgent pre-sales requests, urgent customer issues, and other customer-driven feature requests, alongside the backend maintenance and integration work that keeps the platform stable. You’ll need to be equally comfortable setting engineering standards, coaching engineers, and triaging competing priorities across time zones. &lt;strong&gt;This is a 100% remote role, with preference for candidates located in Cheltenham, UK&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and grow engineering teams based in the US, UK, and APAC, providing hands-on people leadership, coaching, and career development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set priorities across urgent pre-sales requests, urgent customer issues, customer feature requests, and backend maintenance/integration work, balancing reactive and proactive work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure continuous, follow-the-sun coverage for urgent customer and pre-sales needs across time zones&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Customer Success and Sales leadership to understand customer and deal-critical needs and translate them into engineering plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product and other Engineering teams to ensure customer-driven work is integrated into the broader platform roadmap&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the team&#39;s engineering quality bar, including code quality, root-cause practices, and long-term fixes over one-off patches&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive hiring, onboarding, and performance management across all three regional teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and refine on-call, escalation, and incident response processes for the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Report on team health, throughput, and customer outcomes to engineering and company leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Remove blockers for your teams and stay close enough to the technical work to make credible calls under pressure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience managing software engineers, ideally across distributed or multi-region teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in cybersecurity, vulnerability management, or threat intelligence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience as a senior or staff software engineer, with credibility to engage in technical discussions and unblock your team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing customer-facing, support, sustaining, or reliability engineering teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to prioritize and sequence competing demands—urgent customer issues, pre-sales asks, and longer-term maintenance work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing teams across multiple time zones and regions, with strong async communication habits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of backend systems, APIs, distributed systems, and cloud infrastructure (AWS preferred)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A customer-obsessed mindset and a track record of turning technical challenges into strong customer outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills, with the ability to work effectively with customers, Sales, Customer Success, and other Engineering teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with data pipelines, ETL systems, or high-volume data processing is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience managing a customer reliability, sustaining, support, or escalation engineering function&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with CVE, NVD, KEV, or exploit intelligence datasets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting pre-sales or deal-critical technical requests&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in high-growth or startup environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe people do their best work when they feel supported, trusted, and valued. VulnCheck offers benefits designed to meet a wide range of needs and lifestyles, tailored to your country of employment:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous, flexible time off&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Retirement/pension plan contributions (e.g., 401k with match in the US; local pension schemes elsewhere)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comprehensive healthcare coverage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous paid parental leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Remote-friendly environment with flexibility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support for home office costs (phone &amp;amp; internet)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ongoing professional development, coaching, and learning resources&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunities for career advancement within a fast-growing team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Specific benefit details vary by country and are confirmed during the offer process.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Join Us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Built on over two decades of cybersecurity experience, our team of experts understands the intricacies of vulnerabilities, their exploitation in the wild, and how to leverage this data to build more effective cybersecurity products that produce better outcomes for organizations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;VulnCheck gives organizations a tactical advantage by providing best-in-class exploit &amp;amp; vulnerability intelligence information. We have a sense of duty to protect the critical infrastructure we rely on including medical devices, power grids and telecommunication networks. We were founded in 2021 in Lexington, Massachusetts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;VulnCheck has a transparent, collaborative, and supportive culture - we are looking for people who have a growth mindset, are curious and innovative. Our team is smart, but humble, hardworking, and supportive.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;VulnCheck is proud to be an Equal Employer Opportunity employer. We do not discriminate based upon race, religion, color, national origin, gender (including pregnancy, childbirth, or related medical conditions), sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, status as a protected veteran, status as an individual with a disability, or other applicable legally protected characteristics. VulnCheck is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with physical and mental disabilities. *Even if your experience doesn’t perfectly align with the job description, we encourage you to apply—we value potential just as much as a perfect resume.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;22&quot;&gt;Our &lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;22&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;4&quot;&gt;Order and Inventory Management Team&lt;/strong&gt; is looking for a &lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;22&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;57&quot;&gt;Support Engineer (f/m/d) - Domain Manager&lt;/strong&gt; on a &lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;22&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;104&quot;&gt;Permanent Contract&lt;/strong&gt; based in &lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;22&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;132&quot;&gt;Lille.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;23&quot;&gt;Passionate about logistics innovation, our team of 10 designs and operates the global digital solutions orchestrating Decathlon&#39;s order and stock flows. Our impact: guaranteeing the right product in the right place at the right time for our stores, warehouses, and marketplaces worldwide. Our challenges: accelerating the group&#39;s digital transformation, integrating new business models (circular economy, wholesale), and preparing the transition to SAP S/4HANA.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;24&quot;&gt;YOUR FUTURE CONTRIBUTION&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;25&quot;&gt;As a &lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;25&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;5&quot;&gt;Support Engineer (f/m/d)&lt;/strong&gt;, you will ensure the stability, efficiency, and evolution of our order and stock orchestration tools. Your core responsibilities include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-path-to-node=&quot;26&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;26,0,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;26,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Run Management &amp;amp; User Commitments:&lt;/strong&gt; Organize daily ticket resolution, ensure service level agreements (stock accuracy KPIs, dispatch timing), and provide dedicated support during peak commercial periods.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;26,1,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;26,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Incident Resolution &amp;amp; Continuous Improvement:&lt;/strong&gt; Perform root cause analysis, enhance monitoring tools (dashboards, control towers), and automate recurring tasks leveraging tech and AI.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;26,2,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;26,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Transformation Projects &amp;amp; SAP:&lt;/strong&gt; Challenge upcoming product features with the project team, drive updates on our SAP ECC module (SD/MM), and help prepare the S/4HANA migration planned for 2028.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;26,3,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;26,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Communication &amp;amp; On-Call Rotations:&lt;/strong&gt; Maintain transparent communication with stakeholders during incidents or maintenance, and participate in on-call rotations for critical operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;27&quot;&gt;WHAT YOU BRING&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul data-path-to-node=&quot;28&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;28,0,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;28,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Education &amp;amp; Background:&lt;/strong&gt; Engineering degree (preferably in Computer Science) or equivalent experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;28,1,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;28,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Functional &amp;amp; Technical Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt; Strong understanding of supply chain processes combined with proven experience on SAP modules (SD and MM).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;28,2,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;28,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Automation Mindset:&lt;/strong&gt; Passion for eliminating manual repetitive tasks, tracking data performance, and integrating AI into daily operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;28,3,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;28,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Soft Skills:&lt;/strong&gt; Team player spirit (&quot;Play Collective&quot;), clear communication, strong prioritization skills, and collaborative leadership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;28,4,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;28,4,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Languages:&lt;/strong&gt; Fluent English is mandatory (daily international scope).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;29&quot;&gt;TECH STACK&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul data-path-to-node=&quot;30&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;30,0,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;30,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;ERP / Systems:&lt;/strong&gt; SAP ECC (SD &amp;amp; MM modules), S/4HANA roadmap.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;30,1,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;30,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Monitoring &amp;amp; Data:&lt;/strong&gt; Operational control towers, ticketing systems, and custom monitoring dashboards.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;31&quot;&gt;WHAT WE OFFER&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul data-path-to-node=&quot;32&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;32,0,0&quot;&gt;Hybrid work organization (up to 2 days of remote work per week);&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;32,2,0&quot;&gt;Equipment provided in line with your role and our sustainability commitments (Mac, Windows, or Chromebook);&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;32,3,0&quot;&gt;A local project team within a global network (international career opportunities);&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;32,4,0&quot;&gt;Continuous learning and development (technical certifications in year one, internal/external training programs);&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;32,5,0&quot;&gt;Comprehensive compensation package (employee stock ownership scheme, monthly/quarterly bonuses).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;34&quot;&gt;OUR COMMITMENT TO INCLUSION AND ACCESSIBILITY&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;35&quot;&gt;At Decathlon, we recognize the immense value that diversity brings to our teams, and we continuously strive to foster and cultivate an inclusive and equitable workplace: this is why Inclusion is one of our Human Fundamentals. We encourage people of all backgrounds and abilities to apply, as we firmly believe that diversity of thought, culture, identity, and lived experience makes us stronger.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;36&quot;&gt;Decathlon is also committed to providing an inclusive and accessible recruitment process for all candidates. If you require any reasonable adjustments during the process, you can request them via the application form; your request will remain confidential and will not affect the outcome of your hiring process.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DECATHLON DIGITAL CONTEXT&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What if technology allowed us to push the boundaries and take sports experiences to new levels? That&#39;s exactly our goal at Decathlon Digital! We are a team of 5,000+ experts in software engineering, product management, data, cloud, and cybersecurity, distributed across Paris, Lille, and Amsterdam. Together, we are creating the largest digital sports platform, leveraging tech innovation from design to value chain optimization, connected experiences and product second life.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Changing the game for good&lt;/strong&gt;. We are in this for the love of sports. And like everything we love, we want it to last. That’s why we are embarking on a journey to create a more sustainable tech model, reducing our direct environmental impact while maintaining a safe, diverse, and inclusive space for all our people to learn and thrive together. Team up with us to design the digital future of sports.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Grafana Labs is the company behind Grafana Cloud, the fully managed observability platform trusted by more than 10,000 organizations to ensure reliability, resolve incidents faster, and optimize telemetry at scale. Built on open source and open standards and designed for interoperability across any stack, Grafana Cloud brings AI to observability and observability to AI, giving teams (and their agents) unified visibility so they can see, understand, and act on all their disparate data, wherever it lives, and move at the speed of their ambitions. Customers, including Anthropic, Bloomberg, NVIDIA, Microsoft, and Salesforce, rely on Grafana Labs. We are a 100% remote company with team members across 40+ countries, backed by leading investors including Lightspeed Venture Partners, Sequoia Capital, GIC, Coatue, J.P. Morgan, CapitalG, and Lead Edge Capital. Learn more at &lt;u&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://grafana.com&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;grafana.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/u&gt; and follow us on &lt;u&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/grafana-labs/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/u&gt; and &lt;u&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://twitter.com/grafana&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;X&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;u&gt;.&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re scaling fast and staying true to what makes us different: an open-source legacy, a global collaborative culture, and a passion for meaningful work. Our team thrives in an innovation-driven environment where transparency, autonomy, and trust fuel everything we do.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You may not meet every requirement, and that’s okay. If this role excites you, we’d love you to raise your hand for what could be a truly career-defining opportunity.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This is a remote opportunity and we would be interested in applicants based in Spain, Ireland, Germany, the UK or Sweden at this time.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Opportunity:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Grafana Observability builds end-to-end observability that spans application, infrastructure, database, browser, and mobile. Our Mobile Observability initiative gives mobile developers first-class instrumentation SDKs that capture traces, metrics, logs, crashes, and user sessions. Our solutions aim to be tightly integrated with OpenTelemetry and Grafana Cloud. We’re building high-performance, low-overhead SDKs that make it easy for teams to connect mobile signals to backend and infra telemetry for true full-stack visibility.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We value open standards, great developer experience, and doing the hard engineering needed to ship reliable software at scale. You may not meet every requirement below. If this role excites you, please raise your hand.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Be Doing:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and evolve mobile instrumentation SDKs for iOS (Swift / Obj-C), prioritizing performance, stability, and a great developer experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and ship SDK features such as session tracking, crash reporting, sampling strategies, automatic context propagation, and OpenTelemetry integrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own projects end-to-end.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Break large, ambiguous problems into incremental deliverables: design modular solutions, ship MVPs, gather feedback, iterate quickly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure quality: automated tests, CI, documentation, and smooth, backwards-compatible upgrade paths.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate cross-functionally with backend, frontend, product, and solutions engineering to ensure cohesive end-to-end observability workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage with the open-source community: review PRs, discuss design proposals, and help guide external contributors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor teammates, participate in technical design discussions and help shape the mobile observability roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Makes You a Great Fit:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re a motivated self-starter with a bias toward action and the ability to run with poorly defined scopes. You can operate autonomously while being highly collaborative.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong mobile engineering experience: with iOS (Swift/Obj-C) and, optionally, Android (Kotlin/Java).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience building or maintaining mobile SDKs, platform libraries, or other developer-facing platform code used by external developers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with performance-sensitive code (startup time, memory, network efficiency) and making pragmatic tradeoffs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with OpenTelemetry (instrumentation, SDKs, collectors) or experience contributing to/maintaining OTel SDKs or similar telemetry libraries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working in a fully remote, globally distributed team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coachable, customer-focused, and passionate about developer experience, you can do more than code: you write docs, mentor others, and shape roadmaps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pragmatic and comfortable navigating ambiguity: you prioritize progress over perfection and iterate quickly based on feedback.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Points For:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contributions to OpenTelemetry, crash reporting libraries, or other observability OSS.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with cross-platform frameworks (React Native, Flutter) or building native bindings/bridges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with mobile security, privacy, or platform integration challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior work on crash aggregation, session replay, or sampling for mobile telemetry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation &amp;amp; Rewards:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In Germany, the compensation range for this role is €97,000 - €121,000. Actual compensation may vary based on level, experience, and skillset as assessed throughout the interview process. All of our roles include Restricted Stock Units (RSUs), giving every team member ownership in Grafana Labs&#39; success. We believe in shared outcomes—RSUs help us stay aligned and invested as we scale globally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(236, 240, 241);&quot;&gt;#LI-Remote&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;*Compensation ranges are country specific. If you are applying for this role from a different location than listed above, your recruiter will discuss your specific market’s defined pay range &amp;amp; benefits at the beginning of the process.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why You’ll Thrive at Grafana Labs:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;100% Remote, Global Culture -&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;As a remote-only company, we bring together talent from around the world, united by a culture of collaboration and shared purpose.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scaling Organization&lt;/strong&gt; – Tackle meaningful work in a high-growth, ever-evolving environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Transparent Communication&lt;/strong&gt; – Expect open decision-making and regular company-wide updates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Innovation-Driven&lt;/strong&gt; – Autonomy and support to ship great work and try new things.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Open Source Roots&lt;/strong&gt; – Built on community-driven values that shape how we work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Empowered Teams&lt;/strong&gt; – High trust, low ego culture that values outcomes over optics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Career Growth Pathways&lt;/strong&gt; – Defined opportunities to grow and develop your career.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Approachable Leadership&lt;/strong&gt; – Transparent execs who are involved, visible, and human.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Passionate People&lt;/strong&gt; – Join a team of smart, supportive folks who care deeply about what they do.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In-Person onboarding &lt;/strong&gt;- We want you to thrive from day 1 with your fellow new ‘Grafanistas’ to learn all about what we do and how we do it.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Balance is Key&lt;/strong&gt; - We operate a global annual leave policy of 30 days per annum. 3 days of your annual leave entitlement are reserved for Grafana Shutdown Days to allow the team to really disconnect. &lt;em&gt;*We will comply with local legislation where applicable.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Opportunity Employer:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;Grafana Labs is an equal opportunities employer. We welcome applications from everyone regardless of race, colour, nationality, origin, caste, sex, gender reassignment identity or expression, sexual orientation, age, religion or belief, disability, veteran status, genetic information, pregnancy, maternity, marital, family or carer status, or any other characteristic which is protected by local law. We believe that equality and diversity build a strong organisation, and we work hard to ensure that is the foundation of our organisation as we grow.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;Grafana Labs may utilize AI tools in its recruitment process to assist in matching information provided in CVs to job postings. The recruitment team will continue to review inbound CVs manually to identify alignment with current openings.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
